# CP12 — Razorpay test mode. Real at the edges.
#
# A credibility beat, not a product. One real payment link, one verified
# webhook, one ledger row carrying a real Razorpay id. Nothing in the simulation
# changes: no arm, no policy, no metric, no prior is touched by this checkpoint.
#
# The claim it buys is the one in DECISIONS.md under "Deliberately borrowed":
# simulated at scale, real at the edges. The batch is 10,000 synthetic cases and
# says so; the object in out/razorpay_demo.json is a real Razorpay test-mode
# payment link, paid over the network, whose webhook arrived through ngrok, was
# verified by HMAC SHA256, and was written to the hash-chained ledger.
#
# The labelling discipline is the substance. Every PaymentLinkRecord carries an
# explicit source — RAZORPAY_TEST_MODE or MOCK_SANDBOX — and the pydantic model
# validates the pairing, so a synthetic record cannot be relabelled as a real
# one. Mock ids wear a `MOCK_plink_` prefix and mock URLs sit on the reserved
# `.invalid` TLD, which means the difference survives being screenshotted.
#
# RAZORPAY_MOCK_MODE defaults to true, so a judge cloning the repo with no
# credentials gets a working demo rather than a stack trace. The opposite
# default is the dangerous one: a missing key that produces a plausible id.

settle/api/__init__.py
settle/api/webhook.py
settle/api/app.py
settle/integrations/__init__.py
settle/integrations/razorpay_client.py
settle/integrations/idempotency.py
tests/test_webhook.py
tests/test_razorpay.py
SPEC.md
README.md
checkpoints/cp12.allowlist

# The demo artefact. Not in the prompt's ALLOWLIST block, but mandated by the
# checkpoint body ("Save the whole thing to out/razorpay_demo.json and commit
# it, so the artefact survives ngrok going away"). `out/*` is gitignored, so it
# needs `git add -f`.
out/razorpay_demo.json

# --- BLOCKED: two things outside this allowlist ----------------------------
#
# 1. The demo runner has no home.
#
#    The checkpoint says a judge cloning the repo must get a working demo with
#    no keys, and RAZORPAY_MOCK_MODE=true delivers that at the library level.
#    But there is no committed entry point to run: the runner that created
#    plink_TWr7e2EFJ8ITvn, polled the ledger and wrote out/razorpay_demo.json
#    lives in the session scratchpad, because this allowlist has no `scripts/`
#    entry and CC does not add files outside it.
#
#    The fix is one `git mv` into `scripts/razorpay_demo.py`, plus a mock-mode
#    default so `python scripts/razorpay_demo.py` with no .env prints a
#    MOCK_SANDBOX record and exits clean. Punya's call, not CC's — it is a new
#    committed file, not an edit to a listed one.
#
# 2. `httpx` is not pinned, so `fastapi.testclient.TestClient` cannot be used.
#
#    tests/test_webhook.py drives the ASGI application directly instead. That
#    was the right answer regardless — it can timestamp `http.response.start`
#    specifically, which is the moment Razorpay's 5-second budget actually
#    stops, and TestClient cannot — but it was forced rather than chosen.
#    Installing httpx into .venv without pinning it in requirements.txt would
#    make the gate green here and red for anyone cloning the repo, which is the
#    one outcome worth refusing. requirements.txt is not on this allowlist.
#
#    No fix needed unless a future checkpoint wants TestClient, in which case
#    the line is `httpx==0.28.1` in requirements.txt.
